  "id": "cross-adaptation",
  "term": "cross-adaptation",
  "definition": "Cross-adaptation is a protective effect in which prior exposure to one mild stressor reduces the harmful impact of a different later stressor. In this source, mild heat shock made later metal exposure less damaging to neurobehavior in nematodes.",
